WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.750
So you've heard me say this is not a rehearsal.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.160
This is this is the emergency.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:14.059
The Postal Service says tens of millions of
ballots, mail in ballots, absentee ballots

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:17.300
are at risk of not being counted.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:24.990
The United States Postal Service is warning
that 46 states and Washington, D.C. in July,

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:30.720
they warned tens of millions of voters might
not have their votes counted because of the

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:38.859
slow mail processing of absentee ballot applications
and eventual ballots that in April.

00:00:38.859 --> 00:00:41.050
Washington Post has the story.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:47.739
That was the earliest sign from the post office
that if they do kneecap them in terms of funding,

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:52.449
which the Trump administration is trying to
do, it could affect ballot delivery.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:57.340
Now, I really need people to understand this
because Donald Trump and Trump is saying something

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:58.719
very different.

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:01.640
The problem here is not the volume of ballots.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.409
OK, please look at the numbers.

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:10.910
Every holiday season, you know, November,
December into New Year, the post office regularly

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:16.120
handles about one point three billion greeting
cards around the country.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:23.630
OK, even if every voter voted by mail, we're
looking at somewhere between 120 and 130 million

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:24.900
people voting.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.250
That's only 10 percent of the normal volume
of greeting cards.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:33.430
OK, if we just let the post office do its
thing, it would have no problem handling mail

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:39.730
in ballots, even if every ballot was by mail
instead of in-person.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.010
But that's not going to be the case.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.480
Only some people are planning to vote absentee
or vote by mail.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:51.840
The problem is, if you cut hours, if you limit
overtime, if you closed down post offices,

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.810
if you shut down mailboxes, if you quote,
reorganize the post office the way Lewis Dejoy

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:02.550
wants to do, you will then cause a problem
for the post office being able to deliver

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.850
and do everything that they have to do.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:11.720
The warning from the post office applies to
186 million potential voters.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.710
Now, not all of those voters are expected
to vote by mail.

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:20.950
So that's why in practice, it will probably
affect tens of millions rather than, you know,

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:26.010
186 million, which is the number of people
that could vote in some of these states.

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.110
It's in blue states.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:28.130
It's in red states.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.390
It's in battleground states like Pennsylvania,
Wisconsin, Michigan.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:35.510
So there's a few suggestions here that are
just commonsense.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:39.910
I'm going to have a story tomorrow, by the
way, my mail.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.030
This is today.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:43.120
Well, I'll mention it.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.120
This is crazy.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:49.930
My absentee ballot application took 14 days
to go three miles.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.050
OK.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.410
I'm going to talk about that tomorrow.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:59.050
But as far as suggestions, request your ballots
as early as you can, return your ballot as

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.849
early as you can.

00:03:00.849 --> 00:03:06.510
It likely will be too late for some people
in some states like it seems that we've reached

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:11.790
a post office kneecapping escape velocity
for lack of a better term.

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:17.060
We are unfortunately looking at a situation
where if you want higher confidence that your

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:18.750
vote will be counted.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.260
You might have to vote in person.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.670
Now, I want to be careful here.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:26.130
I'm not suggesting anybody do anything unsafe,
but I'm talking about wearing a mask and all

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:27.690
of that stuff.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:33.030
What I am saying is we're hearing from the
post office itself that they are being sabotaged

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:34.030
or sabotaged.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:38.760
Edged as as William Shatner says, and this
administration is trying to find a way for

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.950
your vote not to count.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:44.030
Now there is some intermediate good news and
this made some some waves over the weekend.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:48.010
And I do want to amplify it in a lot of places.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:53.060
If you get your ballot in the mail, you don't
have to send it in through the mail.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.310
You can drop it off.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.140
And different municipalities have different
places.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.790
Town hall, city hall, different municipal
offices.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:02.670
Figure out the specifics in your community.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:08.020
In other places, if it's 10 days before the
election and you don't have your ballot, for

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.250
example, you might have to vote in person
to make sure your vote is going to be counted.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:13.250
And that's horrifying.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.710
I don't want to pretend that that's not a
possibility.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:19.730
But because it is, Trump is against funding
the post office.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:25.340
His postmaster general has reassigned 23 postal
executives and is sort of circling the wagons

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:27.220
and consolidating power.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.380
They are talking about the post office like
it's a business when really it's a public

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.380
service.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:33.580
You don't say we can't do it.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:37.800
You say, well, okay, what do we have to do
to make sure that they can do it?

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.750
That's what a normal president would do.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:42.540
This president says, let's make sure that
they can't do it.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.090
So really, keep in mind that this local drop
off might be a good idea.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.139
I checked in Boston.

00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:49.370
How does it work in Boston?

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:50.370
In Boston?

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:54.340
The election Web site says if you want to
return your ballot in person, you can do that

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:59.220
anytime city hall is open, but you've got
